Verse 1:
[D/F#]I know [A7]not why [G]God’s [F#m]wondrous [D]grace
[D]To me [A]He [D/A]hath made [A7/G]known,

Refrain:
[A7]But "I [F#m]know whom [A]I have [Em]believed, [D/F#]and am persuaded [G/D]that [D]His is able
[A7/C#]To keep [G/D]that [D/A]which I've committed [G/D]Unto [A7]Him against that day."

Verse 2:
[D/F#]I know not [A7]how this saving [G]faith [F#m]To me He [D]did impart,
[D]Nor how believing [A]in [A7]His [D/A]word Wrought peace within [A7/G]my heart.

Verse 3:
[D/F#]I know not [A7]how the Spirit [G]moves, [F#m]Convincing [D]men of sin,
[D]Revealing Jesus [A7]through the [D/A]word, Creating [A7/G]faith in Him.

Verse 4:
[D/F#]I know not [A7]when my Lord may [G]come, [F#m]At night or [D]noonday fair,
[D]Nor if I walk [A]the vale [A7]with [D/A]Him, Or meet Him [A7/G]in the air.
